⟦ focus_format | FOCUS-FORMAT-v1 | vsm-1.2.1 | 2026-10-30T00:59:27Z ⟧

@vsm 1.2.1
@status active

// Short-note contract for current_focus.json (A-7, D-03 2026-10-01).
// A focus file is a signal surface: readers truncate >2000 chars
// (LCC-07/CYCLE-CLOSE/EPISTEMIC were unreadable at a glance).

entry = {
  ref:     string,        // non-empty, unique in file
  status:  "active" | "paused" | "done",
  note:    string,        // non-empty, max 500 chars
  started_at: iso_utc_z,  // YYYY-MM-DDTHH:MM:SSZ — code-generated (see D-30)
  updated_at: iso_utc_z,
  detail:  string?,       // reference to archived long note
  agent_id: string?,      // optional producer tag
}

// D-30 (0a/0b, decision S5 2026-10-07): timestamps must be generated
// by code (get_timestamp nudges generation off round seconds). The
// `:00` seconds shape, canonical proxy for hand-typing:
//   forward (>= 2026-10-07) -> VIOLATION, gate rejects
//   historical (< cutoff)   -> advisory only, aggregated one line,
//                              never rewritten (16 across 12 entries,
//                              2026-09-22..10-03, real instants)
//
// Long detail lives in state/focus_details/<ref>.md (runtime, local —
// gitignored: same boundary as current_focus itself, clones start []).
// Enforcement: gate focus-format (gate #15, A-7/D-03, D-30a) —
//   check("") validates the live file (advisory `:00` on stderr, rc=0);
//   negative_case = post-cutoff entry with hand-typed `:00` seconds
//   must always fail. Wall-note leg (501 chars) + grandfathered leg
//   stay covered by check-level tests. Live tests:
//   gate_suite/tests/test_focus_format.py
⟦ /focus_format ⟧
